module nhd-criminal-local-rules.local-rules

import core.authority.{ CaseOrder }
import core.frcrimp45.{ frcrimp45 }

// The District of New Hampshire's own criminal periods. Time periods are
// determined under FRCrimP 45(a); FRCrimP 45(c) applies only to periods
// running from service, never to periods running from filing (D.N.H.
// LCrR 45.1). No trigger here carries a service method. The civil and
// general local rules listed in LCrR 1.1(d), LR 7.1(a) and (c)-(f) among
// them, also apply in criminal actions; their periods and page limits are
// lit/nhd's and are not restated here.
//
// Periods that are FRCrimP periods stay in lit/frcrimp and are only named
// here: objections to the initial presentence report are delivered within
// 14 days after receiving it, and an objection not made in time is waived
// unless its basis was not reasonably available (D.N.H. LCrR 32.1(e);
// FRCrimP 32(f)(1)).
//
// Conditions that are not deadlines from an event stay in notes: the court
// sets the trial date at the arraignment (D.N.H. LCrR 10.1); in a complex
// case LCrR 12.1(a), 12.1(b), 16.1(b) and 16.1(c) do not apply and the
// court sets the discovery and motion dates at the status conference
// (LCrR 10.2); a defendant pleading guilty without a written plea
// agreement submits an executed Acknowledgment and Waiver of Rights on or
// before the change-of-plea hearing (LCrR 11.1); objections to motions in
// limine and to exhibit lists are filed on the day of trial (LCrR 12.1(c),
// 16.1(g)); exhibits are delivered to the clerk's office at least one day
// before the start of evidence (LCrR 16.1(g)); the final pretrial
// conference is held approximately 7 days before trial (LCrR 17.1.1);
// jury instruction requests are filed no later than the first day of
// trial (LCrR 30.1); if the court delays sentencing, the presentence
// disclosure, objection and revised-report dates are continued
// automatically (LCrR 32.1(a)); counts unresolved at sentencing are deemed
// dismissed with prejudice unless reserved (LCrR 48.1). A defense motion
// to continue trial carries the defendant's speedy-trial waiver or
// counsel's certification (LCrR 12.1(d)).
//
// The earlier D.N.H. criminal outline's FRCrimP flow and its decisions
// (United States v. Salerno, Brady v. Maryland, Barker v. Wingo, Zedner
// v. United States, Boykin v. Alabama, Missouri v. Frye, Jackson v.
// Virginia, United States v. Booker, Roe v. Flores-Ortega, Garza v.
// Idaho) are FRCrimP, Speedy Trial Act or constitutional authority and
// belong to lit/frcrimp; they are removed here: no reporter text is
// vendored.

/// The arraignment (D.N.H. LCrR 10.3, 12.1(a), 16.1(b), (c)).
event Arraigned()
/// The court determines at the arraignment that the case is likely to be
/// unusually complex (D.N.H. LCrR 10.2).
event ArraignedComplexCase()
/// A Notice for Expedited Plea and Sentencing Hearing is filed with a
/// final plea agreement or an Acknowledgement and Waiver of Rights in a
/// reentry-after-deportation case (D.N.H. LCrR 11.2(a), (b)).
event ExpeditedNoticeFiled()
/// The expedited plea and sentencing hearing is scheduled (D.N.H. LCrR
/// 11.2(c)).
event ExpeditedHearingScheduled()
/// A motion is filed (D.N.H. LCrR 12.1(f)).
event MotionFiled()
/// An order granting an assented-to motion to extend the time to indict
/// (D.N.H. LCrR 12.1(e)).
event ExtensionToIndictGranted()
/// The date set for trial (D.N.H. LCrR 12.1(b), (c), 16.1, 24.1).
event TrialScheduled()
/// The commencement of a proceeding at which a witness is expected to
/// testify (D.N.H. LCrR 16.1(e)).
event ProceedingScheduled()
/// The entry of a plea of guilty or nolo contendere, or a guilty verdict
/// by a jury or the court (D.N.H. LCrR 32.1(a), (c)).
event GuiltEstablished()
/// The scheduled sentencing date (D.N.H. LCrR 32.1(d), (g), (i)).
event SentencingHearingScheduled()
/// The disposition of a case in which counsel was appointed under the
/// Criminal Justice Act (D.N.H. LCrR 44.1(b)).
event CjaDisposition()

/// D.N.H. LCrR 10.2: in a case the court finds at the arraignment likely
/// to be unusually complex, the court schedules a status conference within
/// 14 days after the arraignment.
deadline complex-case-status-conference: 14.days after ArraignedComplexCase() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D.N.H. LCrR 10.2"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.N.H. LCrR 10.3: counsel confer to discuss discovery within 7 days
/// after the arraignment.
deadline post-arraignment-meeting: 7.days after Arraigned() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D.N.H. LCrR 10.3"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.N.H. LCrR 11.2(b): the expedited plea and sentencing hearing is
/// scheduled within 45 days after the filing of the Notice with the plea
/// agreement or the Acknowledgement and Waiver of Rights, as close as
/// possible to the end of the period. These deadlines supersede LCrR
/// 32.1's in such cases (LCrR 11.2(e)).
deadline expedited-hearing: 45.days after ExpeditedNoticeFiled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D.N.H. LCrR 11.2(b); D.N.H. LCrR 11.2(e)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.N.H. LCrR 11.2(c): the probation office discloses the abbreviated
/// presentence investigation report no later than 5 days before the
/// scheduled expedited plea and sentencing hearing.
deadline expedited-psr-disclosure: 5.days before ExpeditedHearingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D.N.H. LCrR 11.2(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.N.H. LCrR 12.1(a): discovery motions are filed within 30 days after
/// the arraignment (not in a complex case, LCrR 10.2).
deadline discovery-motions: 30.days after Arraigned() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D.N.H. LCrR 12.1(a); D.N.H. LCrR 10.2"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.N.H. LCrR 12.1(b): dispositive and evidentiary motions (motions to
/// dismiss and to suppress among them, motions in limine not) are filed no
/// later than 21 days before trial (not in a complex case, LCrR 10.2).
deadline dispositive-motions: 21.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D.N.H. LCrR 12.1(b); D.N.H. LCrR 10.2"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.N.H. LCrR 12.1(c): motions in limine are filed no later than 7 days
/// before trial.
deadline motions-in-limine: 7.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D.N.H. LCrR 12.1(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.N.H. LCrR 12.1(e): with an assented-to motion to extend the time to
/// indict, or within 10 days after the order granting it, defense counsel
/// files the defendant's signed speedy-trial waiver or the LCrR 12.1(d)
/// certification.
deadline indictment-extension-waiver: 10.days after ExtensionToIndictGranted() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D.N.H. LCrR 12.1(e)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.N.H. LCrR 12.1(f): unless the FRCrimP or the local rules provide
/// otherwise, an objection and memorandum in opposition to a motion is
/// filed within 14 days from the date the motion is filed; otherwise
/// objections are deemed waived and the court may act on the motion.
deadline objection-period: 14.days after MotionFiled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D.N.H. LCrR 12.1(f)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.N.H. LCrR 16.1(b)(1); 16.1(c): within 14 days after the arraignment,
/// unless the parties agree on another date or the defendant timely
/// declines, the government discloses the FRCrimP 16(a)(1) information and
/// any evidence of interception of the defendant's communications.
deadline government-routine-discovery: 14.days after Arraigned() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D.N.H. LCrR 16.1(b); D.N.H. LCrR 16.1(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.N.H. LCrR 16.1(b)(2): within 30 days after the arraignment, unless
/// the parties agree on another date or the defendant declined reciprocal
/// discovery, the defendant discloses the FRCrimP 16(b) information.
deadline defendant-routine-discovery: 30.days after Arraigned() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D.N.H. LCrR 16.1(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.N.H. LCrR 16.1(b)(3): later identified expert witnesses and later
/// obtained FRCrimP 16(a)(1)(G)(iii) and (b)(1)(C)(iii) material are
/// disclosed no later than 30 days before trial.
deadline later-expert-disclosure: 30.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D.N.H. LCrR 16.1(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.N.H. LCrR 16.1(b)(3): rebuttal expert witnesses and their FRCrimP
/// 16(a)(1)(G)(iii) material are disclosed no later than 15 days before
/// trial.
deadline rebuttal-expert-disclosure: 15.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D.N.H. LCrR 16.1(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.N.H. LCrR 16.1(d): the government discloses Brady and Giglio material
/// at least 21 days before trial; for good cause it may seek approval to
/// disclose later.
deadline exculpatory-disclosure: 21.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D.N.H. LCrR 16.1(d)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.N.H. LCrR 16.1(e): the government discloses witness statements
/// (FRCrimP 26.2(f); 18 U.S.C. § 3500) at least 7 days before the
/// proceeding at which the witness is expected to testify, unless it
/// determines that later disclosure is allowed by Rule 26.2 and § 3500.
deadline witness-statements: 7.days before ProceedingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D.N.H. LCrR 16.1(e)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.N.H. LCrR 16.1(f): the government discloses the general nature of
/// any Fed. R. Evid. 404(b) evidence at least 7 days before trial.
deadline rule-404b-notice: 7.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D.N.H. LCrR 16.1(f)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.N.H. LCrR 16.1(g): the parties exchange and file exhibit lists at
/// least 7 days before trial.
deadline exhibit-lists: 7.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D.N.H. LCrR 16.1(g)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.N.H. LCrR 16.1(h): the parties file a statement on the use of the
/// Jury Evidence Recording System at least 7 days before trial.
deadline jers-statement: 7.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D.N.H. LCrR 16.1(h)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.N.H. LCrR 16.1(i): the parties exchange and file witness lists at
/// least 7 days before trial; for good cause the court may allow a later
/// date.
deadline witness-lists: 7.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D.N.H. LCrR 16.1(i)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.N.H. LCrR 24.1: requests for special voir dire are filed no later
/// than 7 days before trial.
deadline special-voir-dire: 7.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D.N.H. LCrR 24.1"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.N.H. LCrR 32.1(a): sentencing occurs without unnecessary delay, but
/// no more than 14 weeks (98 days) after the guilty plea or verdict,
/// unless good cause justifies a later date.
deadline sentencing-period: 98.days after GuiltEstablished() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D.N.H. LCrR 32.1(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.N.H. LCrR 32.1(c): no later than 14 days after a plea or verdict of
/// guilty, the government provides the probation office a written version
/// of the facts, including all relevant conduct.
deadline government-version-of-facts: 14.days after GuiltEstablished() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D.N.H. LCrR 32.1(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.N.H. LCrR 32.1(d): the probation officer discloses the initial
/// presentence report no later than 42 days before the scheduled
/// sentencing date. FRCrimP 32(e)(2)'s own period (lit/frcrimp
/// psr-disclosure) is not restated.
deadline initial-psr-disclosure: 42.days before SentencingHearingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D.N.H. LCrR 32.1(d)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.N.H. LCrR 32.1(g): the probation officer provides the revised
/// presentence report, the addendum and the proposed sentencing options and
/// supervision conditions to the court and the parties no later than 14
/// days before the scheduled sentencing date.
deadline revised-psr-disclosure: 14.days before SentencingHearingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D.N.H. LCrR 32.1(g)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.N.H. LCrR 32.1(i): a motion for a departure or variance, or a
/// sentencing memorandum (with any objection to the proposed sentencing
/// options and supervision conditions), is filed no later than 10 days
/// before the scheduled sentencing hearing.
deadline sentencing-memorandum: 10.days before SentencingHearingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D.N.H. LCrR 32.1(i)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.N.H. LCrR 32.1(i): a response to a sentencing memorandum or a motion
/// for a departure or variance is filed no later than 4 days before the
/// scheduled sentencing hearing.
deadline sentencing-response: 4.days before SentencingHearingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D.N.H. LCrR 32.1(i)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.N.H. LCrR 44.1(b): counsel appointed under the Criminal Justice Act
/// file the completed voucher for fees and expenses as soon as possible,
/// but no later than 45 days from the date of disposition.
deadline cja-voucher: 45.days after CjaDisposition() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D.N.H. LCrR 44.1(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}
